; BrailleForum.inix -- how this database opens, and how its tables are heard.
;
; THE ACB BRAILLE FORUM, SEARCHABLE. Every issue of the American Council of the Blind's magazine that acb.org offers
; electronically, with its sister the ACB E-Forum: one row an issue in issues, one row an article in articles. An
; article's words are in body when ACB published it as a web page (Markdown, with ACB's own headings, lists and
; links), and in text when it came only from the issue's plain-text file. format says which.
;
; FIND ONE. The row speaks title, author and published (the year and month). Keywords (Control+K) and Filter Records
; work as on any table. For ranked full-text searches -- a phrase, words near each other, words starting alike --
; run one of the saved searches here, or adapt one from Searches.md beside this file. kind tells an article from the
; masthead, the table of contents and the standing notices every issue repeats; the searches keep kind = 'article'.
;
; READ ONE. Alt+Right on an issue goes to its articles, in the issue's order (position). Control+Shift+U opens the
; article's page at acb.org, or the issue's text file. The reading_list report writes up the marked articles.
;
; scripts\makeBrailleForum in DbDo's development folder builds this file from acb.org; the build runs it when the
; database is missing. The database stays on that computer: it is not on GitHub and not in the installer.
;
; Look is each table's default columns and prime its default order; a table's saved columns, order and filter are
; written here only when a person chooses them.

[Database]

InitialTable = articles

[Table:articles]

; SelectFields, 25 November 2026: who wrote what, and when.
SelectFields = title, author, published

[Table:issues]

SelectFields = title, articles, words

[Table:defs]


[Table:maps]
